{"id":"chatcmpl-a64652dd-0810-4c57-b56d-af12c5cd69ff","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229776,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a visual medical image interpretation workflow where the key challenge is laterality determination (left vs. right). The successful strategy involved targeted region-of-interest zooming to inspect anatomical landmarks, followed by explicit verification of patient orientation and side-of-origin before committing to an answer. The pattern generalizes to any image-based classification task where spatial orientation and side-specific findings must be distinguished.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a task requires distinguishing left vs. right or other spatially-opposed options, zoom into the relevant anatomical/visual region to confirm the side of origin relative to patient orientation rather than relying on the full-image first impression.\",\n    \"Before finalizing a laterality-dependent answer, explicitly verify both that the finding is present on the claimed side AND that no competing finding exists on the opposite side.\",\n    \"Use a targeted crop/zoom action early to resolve ambiguity in small or subtle features (e.g., catheter entry point, tip location) that are hard to assess at full resolution.\",\n    \"Ground the final answer in anatomical landmarks (clavicle, midline, shoulder) rather than raw image coordinates, since image-left/right may not match patient-left/right.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Zoom into the region containing the finding, identify anatomical landmarks to establish patient orientation, and confirm the finding's side relative to those landmarks before answering.\",\n    \"Spatially-opposed classification (left/right, above/below)\": \"Treat laterality as a two-part check: confirm presence on the claimed side and absence on the opposite side; use landmarks, not pixel coordinates.\",\n    \"Subtle-feature verification\": \"When the discriminating feature is small (line entry, tip, marker), crop and magnify that region before deciding, then re-verify against the full image context.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm patient orientation using anatomical landmarks (e.g., clavicle, midline) so image-side maps correctly to patient-side.\",\n    \"Verify the finding originates on the claimed side and that no equivalent finding is present on the opposite side before finalizing.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":495,"total_tokens":942,"completion_tokens":447,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":495},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":447}}}